# Provider-B worktree — DeepSeek generation, OpenAI retrieval.
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in DEEPSEEK_API_KEY. Secrets only:
# policy (models, endpoints, datasource, routing) lives in governed_bi.toml with
# this arm's overrides in governed_bi.local.toml. A real shell variable always
# beats `.env`.
#
# WHAT THIS WORKTREE IS FOR
# -------------------------
# One variable: the generator. The corpus is a byte-identical copy of the trees
# the 20260801 gpt-5.6-luna ladder served (Opus-built, BUILD_COMPLETE markers
# intact), and the embedding channel stays on OpenAI. Move the embedder too and
# the schema shortlist moves along with the answer, so neither effect would be
# attributable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Named by [models].api_key_env. The chat client is pointed at
# https://api.deepseek.com ([models].base_url) and asks for deepseek-v4-flash
# over the OpenAI Responses API, which DeepSeek implements.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...

# Named by [models].embedding_api_key_env. The EMBEDDER only — pointed at
# https://api.openai.com/v1 ([models].embedding_base_url) for
# text-embedding-3-large, the same model and endpoint the luna arm used.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Named by [datasource].dsn_env. The obfuscated BIRD Postgres (local docker,
# port 5435). Note the eval driver does NOT read this variable itself — pass the
# DSN as `--pg-dsn`, because that flag's own default carries no password.
PG_RENAME_DECOY_DSN=host=127.0.0.1 port=5435 dbname=bird user=bird password=...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT set this
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_BASE_URL would redirect the chat client AND the embedder together —
# both build an OpenAI-shaped client and both read it. That is exactly why
# [models].base_url / embedding_base_url exist: DeepSeek serves the chat model
# and does not serve text-embedding-3-large, so a single env var cannot express
# this configuration. Set the endpoints in TOML; leave this unset.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracing — LangSmith, and only LangSmith
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Langfuse was removed on 2026-08-02. LangSmith bills ONE trace per root
# invocation, so a whole agentic turn (dozens of nested runs) costs one trace and
# a 20-question debug run costs 20 of the 5,000/month free tier. Nothing to
# self-host, no callback to wire: LangChain reads these two variables itself.
#
# Off by default. When on, traces carry run inputs and outputs IN FULL — tool
# messages, row previews, governed context. That is intended: this repo is not
# production and sensitive columns are filtered at the datasource before they can
# reach a tool message. A production deployment would need a masking layer at the
# tracer seam; there is none here, deliberately.
# LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=lsv2_...
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=governed-bi
